      "headline": "Soft robot sets land speed record using pneumatic logic",
      "body": "UC San Diego researchers built a 3D-printed soft robot that cycles its legs using pneumatic logic gates instead of a microcontroller. The air-driven control lets it switch quickly between abduction and adduction, and it can even run on water. The team had to modify a commercial printer to work with the TPE material.",
      "why": "It shows soft robots can gain speed through clever mechanical control rather than complex electronics, hinting at more agile and resilient soft machines.",
