      "headline": "Single-chip GPU sends video over a jumper wire",
      "body": "Bitluni's CH570-based USB GPU generates analog video with PWM and appears to a computer as a USB CDC device. While testing, he found a TV in wireless reception mode could pick up the PWM signal from a jumper wire. He is now exploring SPI and overclocking to transmit a PAL color signal.",
      "why": "It shows how a microcontroller's unintended RF emissions can become a feature, hinting at new ways to send video without dedicated transmitters.",
